audits3.summary:
I audited ch00–ch07 adversarially through the theory lens and checked every Definition, Proposition and Theorem of ch04–ch07 by hand. I also ran a numerical check of the Schwinger-integral expansions in Lemma c4-integrals: the remainders converge.

None of the computed numbers has a sign or normalisation error:
- quadratic counterterm: 9/4, −1, 4, −1;
- logarithmic counterterm: 6,6,10,10,1,1,1,1 (cubic) and 8,8,8 (quartic), including the field-counting sign;
- QME obstruction: −27/8 = (27/16)·(−2);
- O(ε) for the scalar bilinears;
- scaling covariance and the Callan–Symanzik form;
- dilatation coefficients 0 and −24 units, giving +3g²N/(4π²) for the trace bilinear (positive, the Konishi value).

The refutations are about accuracy of statements and missing proofs:
- the ch00 summary of Chapter 2 is out of date;
- the acyclicity is overclaimed;
- the locality/power-counting lemma that ch04 and ch05 rely on is never proved;
- gauge-variant operators are mishandled in Prop c6-classical, the Step-2 identification and Rem c7-internal;
- the operator cocycle condition Q O[∞] = 0 is neither computed nor assumed;
- Cor c7-K drops the rotation terms for the letters A|_V and λ.

There are 15 findings: 6 moderate (5 refuted as stated, 1 missing hypothesis) and 9 minor. Each has a location and a concrete fix. The results are written to qa/audit_theory3.json.

audits3.key_results:
VERDICTS (lens: theory). Full detail is in qa/audit_theory3.json.

CH00 (accuracy of the summary): PARTLY REFUTED.
- T3-01: l.57 says the Chapter-2 components of arities 1–3 hold "for su(2) at sampled generators, with a probability bound". ch02 Thm c2-master now proves them exactly on a basis for su(2) and su(3), and the colour-reduction lemma extends this to every g.
- T3-02: l.26–30 claims "contracting homotopy ⇒ Q-exact away from finitely many zero-mode classes". This is false as stated:
  - P(0,∞)⋆ does not preserve E_c, so the homotopy does not pass to functionals of E_c;
  - acyclicity is proved only on moment-free Schwartz sections;
  - the zero-mode classes are infinitely many;
  - the list is incomplete: φ = x₁dx₂ in the A|_V slot gives a nontrivial class.
- T3-13: l.42 says every coefficient is carried by boundary edges. That is overstated: the obstruction also uses K_ε−K₀ edges and −QI^CT vertices.
- T3-07: the Chapter-7 bullet is overstated.
- All numbers in the Ch3–Ch6 bullets and in the table match the chapters.

CH04:
- Confirmed:
  - the boundary method (Prop c4-boundary, Cor c4-sing, Lemmas c4-gauss and c4-integrals; the last checked numerically);
  - all five worked two-point examples, recomputed by hand;
  - the quadratic totals, which reproduce the standard Feynman-gauge N=4 Z-factors as a sanity check;
  - the field-renormalisation theorem: the sign of Lemma c4-count was rederived and the weights 2, 4, 1 fit all 15 sector multiples;
  - Cor c4-coupling (the decomposition is unique and the coupling direction is legitimate);
  - D_ε and Prop c4-defectflow, signs checked;
  - Thm c4-obstruction: no log ε, the ε⁻¹ parts cancel, finite part −27/8;
  - Thm c4-finite and Prop c4-K, by hand.
- REFUTED as stated (T3-03): Lemma c4-weights is used without its locality hypothesis. Prop c4-structure and Rem c4-thmB rely on locality and power counting for the graphs with five or more legs, which is neither computed nor proved. "Is the counterterm of [C07, Thm B]" is an overclaim. Uniqueness of I^CT, used later in Lemma c6-ct, is never stated.

CH05:
- Confirmed: definitions of O(ε) and O[∞], the uniqueness argument, letters O(ε) = O, and graphs (a)–(f) recomputed (vacuum 2ħ dim g (w₁,w₂)/(16π²ε); (e) 2O − 2(w₁,w₂)·trace; (f) 2O; (c)+(d) = 0). Thm c5-Oeps confirmed.
- REFUTED:
  - Prop c5-local item 3 and the chapter intro repeat the acyclicity overclaim (T3-02).
  - Prop c5-thmB is stated for every local operator but its existence step is proved only for the operators computed (T3-03).
- Minor: the dominated-convergence step and the [C07, Thm A] citation in Lemma c5-log (T3-08); the census proof omits the single-λ leg (T3-12); "modulo constants" in ch03 conflicts with the vacuum term kept in O(ε) (T3-10).

CH06:
- Confirmed:
  - scaling covariance;
  - Lemma c6-ct;
  - Callan–Symanzik Thm c6-CS, sign checked by explicit momentum scaling;
  - Lemma c6-bvexact and Cor c6-fieldredef;
  - Thm c6-dil for the scalar bilinears.
- Dilatation signs and normalisation confirmed:
  - 2(E + w_O + coef) for Δ = 2E of [SW, (17)];
  - −(E + w_O + coef) for −E of [SW, (3)];
  - coef = γ_O = 2b + 2γ_φ with γ_φ = −4·unit;
  - traceless 0; trace −24·unit = +3g²N/(4π²);
  - boundary tables: −20 + 4 − 16 + 8 = −24 and 4 + 4 − 16 + 8 = 0.
- REFUTED (T3-04): Prop c6-classical and the identification eq c6-step2 fail for gauge-variant O. They omit the trees with one (Q+{I,−})O vertex and one S^(1)(x₁) vertex. For the A|_V letter this is already nonzero at ħ⁰ (a longitudinal piece). The linear coefficients for ι_wA, λ, c are unaffected, and the bilinears are unaffected.
- GAP (T3-05): the operator cocycle condition Q O[∞] = 0 at arity 0 and order ħ is neither computed, assumed nor listed in Step 2. The one-loop coefficients are unaffected, because a finite weight-w_O counterterm is scale covariant.
- Minor: the A|_V "transverse part" coefficient is ambiguous and the cancellation in Rem c6-AV is not computed (T3-11); the sign convention for inserting an odd F is undefined (T3-09).

CH07:
- Confirmed: Lemma c7-image, Lemma c7-weights, Prop c7-cov, Cor c7-equiv, Cor c7-schur, Prop c7-dil ([v.,Q^GF] = −4Q^GF, (v.⊗1+1⊗v.)P = 4εL_ε, consistent with σ_λ), Prop c7-susy, Prop c7-select under its hypotheses, Cor c7-Q and Cor c7-S, and Rem c7-KDelta ([K,P] bracket and arity-2 identity).
- REFUTED (T3-06): the second bullet of Cor c7-K omits the rotation terms (X, ι_{a v₂}A|_V) and (ζ, ρ(q(a))λ) for the letters A|_V and λ, where a is the antisymmetric part of dv(x₀).
- Overstated:
  - the intro "proves both statements", whereas "can be chosen classical" appears only in a Remark (T3-07);
  - Rem c7-internal's identity fails for gauge-variant O (T3-04);
  - "the obstruction is a local functional" in the road ahead (T3-15).

Totals: 6 moderate (5 refuted as stated, 1 missing hypothesis) and 9 minor.
